{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The problem was in `truncate_slug` in `repo/slug.py`. Report URLs are built from hyphenated titles and then cut to a max length; slicing at the limit often stopped right after a `-`, so you got slugs like `my-report-`.\n\n**Fix:** After `text[:limit]`, strip trailing hyphens with `.rstrip(\"-\")`. For example, `truncate_slug(\"my-report-title\", 10)` is now `my-report` instead of `my-report-`.\n\nAll tests in `tests/` pass. `old_slugify` and `slug_summary` in `repo/rows.py` use the same helper, so they pick up the fix automatically."}]},"session_id":"6ad366aa-d101-4f30-b995-eba5a8f602cb"}
